---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import VoxelScene from "../components/VoxelScene.astro";
import { email, whatsapp, x, duniaVideo, games } from "../data.js";
---

<Base
  title="Artifisi"
  description="Artifisi is a small company in Kuala Lumpur. We build Dunia, an SDK that turns gameplay into training data for robotics and physical AI. We also make games."
>
  <VoxelScene />
  <h1>Artifisi</h1>
  <p>
    We are a small company in Kuala Lumpur. Two people. Most of our time goes into Dunia, an SDK that
    records what happens inside a game and turns it into training data for robots and other physical AI.
    We also make our own games.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">Dunia</h2>
  <p>
    Robots learn from examples. They need to see the scene, what the agent did and what happened next,
    over and over. That data is slow and expensive to collect in the real world. A game engine already
    knows all of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dunia hooks into the engine and saves state, inputs and outcomes at each decision while someone plays.
    Every step comes out labelled. Right now the MVP runs inside our own demo game. Here it is:
  </p>
  <div class="video">
    <iframe src={duniaVideo.embed} title="Dunia demo video" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
  </div>
  <p class="small">Video doesn't load? <a href={duniaVideo.link}>Open it on Google Drive</a>.</p>
  <p>
    We want a few robotics or data teams to try it with. If that's you, <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Dunia`}>email me</a>.
    There's a bit more on the <a href="/projects/dunia">Dunia page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="games">Games</h2>
  <p>
    We make games because we like making games, and because Dunia needs games to run inside. All three
    are our own IP.
  </p>
  <div>
    {
      games.map((g) => (
        <div class="game">
          {g.image ? <img src={g.image} alt={g.name} loading="lazy" width="720" height="405" /> : <div class="noimg" />}
          <div>
            <h3>
              {g.name}
              <span class="status">{g.status}</span>
            </h3>
            <p>{g.blurb}</p>
            <p class="small">
              {g.links.map((l, i) => (
                <>
                  {i > 0 && " · "}
                  <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>
                </>
              ))}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2 id="about">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    I'm Raja Hafify. I spent twelve years writing software at startups and at AirAsia, and the last two on
    AI work. I started Artifisi in 2023 and went full time in 2025. I built Orbwalker on my own in three
    months.
  </p>
  <p>
    Hazmi Faiz is our creative director. He comes from motion graphics and digital media, and he handles how
    our games look.
  </p>
  <p>We got Malaysia Digital status in September 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, or WhatsApp
    <a href={whatsapp.href}>{whatsapp.label}</a>. We're also <a href={x.href}>{x.label}</a> on X.
  </p>
</Base>
